<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henri Coiffier de Ruzé, Marquis of Cinq-Mars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1620">1620</a>–<a href="/years/1642">1642</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Cinq-Mars</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henri Coiffier de Ruzé, Marquis of Cinq-Mars, was a favourite of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiii-of-france">Louis XIII of France</a>. Encouraged by the king's brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaston-duke-of-orleans">Gaston of Orléans</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederic-maurice-de-la-tour-dauvergne">Duke of Bouillon</a>, he plotted to overthrow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardinal-richelieu">Cardinal Richelieu</a> and made a secret treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. When the conspiracy was discovered in 1642 he was tried and beheaded at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henri-coiffier-de-ruze-marquis-of-cinq-mars.jpg" alt="Henri Coiffier de Ruzé, Marquis of Cinq-Mars" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:(Narbonne)_Portait_d%27Henri_d%27Effiat,_Marquis_de_Cinq_Mars_-_Anonyme_-_Mus%C3%A9e_des_Beaux-Arts_de_Narbonne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
